<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Silis</span></b> , is, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of several rivers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> I. q. Jaxartes, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 16,
				18, § 49</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> I. q. Tanais, <i>the Don</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 7,
				7, § 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>A river in the Venetian territories</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 18,
				22, § 126</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
